<% content_for :title, "AWSM Privacy" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "public-site" %>
<%= render "shared/public_header" %>
<main class="site-container trust-page">
  <header class="trust-page__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Factual product explanation · not a legal policy</p>
    <h1>What stays local. What a server can see.</h1>
    <p>This page describes AWSM's current technical behavior. An operator of a self-hosted server controls that deployment and its logs.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <section><h2>Local Capture and Vault content</h2><p>Captured page content, local projections, decryption keys, and the Recovery Phrase belong to the client environment. A local-only Vault does not require an Account or Coordination Server.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Search and optional embeddings</h2><p>Keyword Search, its encrypted local materializations, and the optional downloaded semantic model stay in the browser. If a user separately configures a remote embedding endpoint, AWSM sends bounded Capture passages from the selected Vault while indexing and sends each submitted Search query to that exact endpoint. The endpoint provider may retain content or charge under its own terms. This opt-in processing is separate from AWSM synchronization and is not local or end-to-end encrypted by AWSM.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Account and session records</h2><p>A Coordination Server stores the Account email, a password digest, browser and API session records, Device certificates, and encrypted key envelopes. The Account password is received by the server for authentication; it is not a Vault decryption password.</p><p>After browser signup or sign-in, AWSM also sets <code>awsm_browser_session_hint</code>, a first-party functional cookie containing only a random opaque value. It is readable by this site's JavaScript so anonymous visitors do not need an Account-status request. It contains no credential or Account data and cannot authenticate you.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Synchronization data</h2><p>The server stores opaque encrypted Vault records and Artifact bytes. It also sees necessary operational metadata such as identifiers, byte counts, request timing, traffic patterns, and IP or access logs. It cannot decrypt Vault content from the stored records.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Public website</h2><p>The AWSM landing and public trust pages include no analytics, tracking pixels, marketing cookies, third-party scripts, or remote fonts. Their shared anonymous response may be cached by the deployment's CDN. The CDN and ordinary server access logs may still receive standard connection and request metadata. Account, signup, and session responses are not shared-cache content.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Export and deletion boundaries</h2><p>Complete Export creates a portable client-held copy. Removing local data affects that browser installation; it cannot erase copies already exported, downloaded to other Devices, or retained under a server's documented deletion process.</p></section>
  </div>
</main>
<%= render "shared/public_footer" %>
